{% comment %}
  A project's logo, inline and the height of the surrounding text, for use right before its name
  (include brand_mark.liquid with name="tubebench", then the word). Projects can also set
  `title_icon:` in their front matter to put it before their title on /projects/ and on the page.

  Inline SVG rather than an <img>, so it sizes with the font, sits on the text line and costs no
  request. Its colours come from CSS (.brand-mark in _sass/_base.scss) so the dark theme can
  switch to the logo's reverse palette. The name next to it carries the meaning, so the mark is
  hidden from screen readers.

  The viewBox is cropped to the drawing (the source logo sits in a 64 x 64 square with empty
  space above and below), so the mark is as tall as the capitals rather than shrunk inside a box.

  The markup is captured and printed on one line: placed at the start of a Markdown paragraph,
  an SVG broken over indented lines could be read as the start of an HTML or code block.
{% endcomment %}
{%- capture brand_svg -%}
  {%- case include.name -%}
    {%- when 'tubebench' -%}
      <svg class="brand-mark brand-mark-tubebench" viewBox="2.5 10.5 59 39" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect class="tb-body-line" x="4" y="34" width="56" height="14" rx="7" fill="none" stroke-width="3"/><rect class="tb-body-fill" x="26" y="34" width="12" height="14"/><g stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"><line class="tb-m1" x1="10" y1="33" x2="10" y2="18"/><line class="tb-m2" x1="18" y1="33" x2="18" y2="18"/><line class="tb-m3" x1="46" y1="33" x2="46" y2="18"/><line class="tb-m4" x1="54" y1="33" x2="54" y2="18"/></g><circle class="tb-m1" cx="10" cy="14" r="3.5"/><circle class="tb-m2" cx="18" cy="14" r="3.5"/><circle class="tb-m3" cx="46" cy="14" r="3.5"/><circle class="tb-m4" cx="54" cy="14" r="3.5"/>
      </svg>
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{{- brand_svg | strip_newlines -}}
